/**
 * \page phigs.def      Read the OpenPHIGS configuration file
 *
 *
 * The PHIGS configuration file allows to change the default behavior of OpenPHIGS.
 *
 * \section global Global options
 * Global options determine general features of the library
 * - \%gs 1                 Use shaders (1) or not (0)
 * - \%vs 420               Vertex shader version, can be 120 or 420
 * - \%fs 420               Fragment shader version, can be 120 or 420
 * - \%pc 1                 print configuration if set to 1. Set to 0 to disable dumping of configuration parameters.
 *
 * \section workstations Workstation specific settings
 * Define one section for each workstation. Each section starts with a \%wk, followed by a positive integer representing the workstation number. Definitions for workstation number 0 set the default for all other workstations. That is, settings following  \%wk 0 are applied to all workstations, \%wk 1 are only applied to workstation 1 and so on. Later definitions usually win. Available parameters depend on the workstation type as well.
 *
 * - \%bs <yes/no>          Backing store, yes or no
 * - \%wn string            Set workstation name to string
 * - \%in string            set workstation icon name to string
 * - \%xe <yes/no>          return x events
 * - \%wr <yes/no>          Window is resizable or not
 * - \%wg 512 512 0 0 1     Window width height px py and border size in pixel
 * - \%wp 0.0 1.0 0.0 1.    Window positition
 * - \%bg  0. 0. 0.         Background color in RGB mode
 * - \%bga 0. 0. 0. 0.5     Background color in RGBA
 * - \%hs 3.                scale factor for hardcopy related work station types
 * - \%ior 0                Ordern Independent Rendering disable (0) /enable (1). Requires shader 420
 * - \%lpp 16               Order Independent Rendering layers per pixel (between 1 and 16). Requires shader 420
 *
 * \note Ordern independent rendering can be quite memory intensive. If enabled for the main window, it makes sense to enable it as well for hardcopy workstation types, if these are used.
 * \bug Not all parameters may be implemented or have an actual effect, depending on the hardware and driver setup
 *
 * \sa phigsf77.h
 *
 * \example phigs.def
 */
